The adapter is released under Apache-2.0, the license of Gemma 4. Training data licenses: {% for k, v in licenses.items() %}{{ k }} ({{ v }} samples){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}; TAT-QA (CC-BY-4.0, Zhu et al. 2021) and FinQA/ConvFinQA (MIT, Chen et al. 2021/2022) provided retention prompts. Benchmarks with non-commercial or unclear terms (Financial PhraseBank, FiQA, FinanceBench, Gold headlines) were used for evaluation only and never trained on; every training sample was 13-gram decontaminated against them.

## Limitations

- Market numbers must come from tools at inference time; the model is not a source of prices or financials, and its knowledge of companies stops at the base model's cut-off.
- Full five-tool analyses exceed the 2 048-token training window, so their final answers were learned from shorter sectioned answers (ADR 0401).
- Synthetic traces have a regular style; real users phrase questions more variously.
- Evaluation suites are small (n = 100–500); differences of a few points are within noise.
- English only. Not financial advice.
